course: dictionary
lesson: 3938
title: Learning a new word from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new even to clever readers. When you meet «fugu», read the words around it. «Pufferfish, called fugu in Japan, have a very strong poison in their liver» tells you that fugu is another name used in Japan for a pufferfish.
explain: The next clue comes from «only chefs with a special licence may prepare fugu». Prepare means to get food ready to eat, and a licence is official permission. So fugu can also mean a dish that only experts are allowed to make. Test it: "only chefs may prepare a pufferfish" still makes sense.
explain: Words like poison, kill and trained are clues too. They show that fugu is dangerous, so you should not guess its meaning and try it. When the context gives a strong warning, read it carefully and check a dictionary if you are unsure.
fact: Fugu means a pufferfish, or a Japanese dish made from it.
fact: The fish has a deadly poison, so only specially trained and licensed chefs may prepare it.
fact: The poison is in parts such as the liver and ovaries.
fact: Some animals make strong toxins to protect themselves, and pufferfish are one example.
fact: «Farm-raised pufferfish can be poison-free», so the risk depends on how the fish was raised.
exercise: «Pufferfish, called fugu in Japan, have poison in the liver.» What is fugu? | *A pufferfish, or a Japanese dish made from it | A coloured paper lantern | A kind of rice | A large Japanese garden
exercise: «Only chefs with a special licence may prepare fugu.» Why must fugu be prepared by experts? | Because it only lives in mountain lakes | Because it is too big to carry | Because it tastes too sweet to cook | *Because the fish contains a deadly poison
exercise: «Only chefs with a special licence may prepare fugu.» What does licence mean here? | A type of fish | A sharp knife used by chefs | *Official permission | A kind of food
test: «One fish can hold enough poison to kill about thirty people.» What does this sentence tell you about fugu? | *It can be deadly, so it must be prepared by experts | It is always poison-free | It is a kind of fruit | It is a safe snack for children
test: A «fugu chef» is a phrase from the lesson. What does it mean? | A fishing boat captain | A chef who only cooks vegetables | A fish that cooks itself | *A chef trained and licensed to prepare fugu
exam: «Farm-raised pufferfish can be poison-free, but only trained chefs may prepare fugu.» What does poison-free mean? | Cooked for a long time | Covered in sharp spikes | Very hungry | *Without poison
